---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Contact
description: Whether you're looking for a job or looking to hire, we're here to help.
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/contact-form.js
  - /assets/js/faq-accordion.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{#
  Hallmark redesign — "The hand-off" (claude_helper/CONTACT-PAGE.md).

  This is the shared endpoint every service-page CTA routes into with a ?role=
  already chosen, so the page's whole job is to make finishing the form feel like a
  conversation already in motion — not a cold front door.

  · Intro stays quiet and narrow — no hero photo. If ?role= is present,
    contact-form.js writes one small "Continuing from · …" meta line under the lead.
  · One consistent 7 / 5 two-column shell from `lg` up. Left: the form in one glass
    panel, steps divided by hairlines. Right: a sticky sidebar — direct lines, the
    "a person, not a queue" note, and the three-node "what happens next" trail — so
    the no-form route stays visible the whole way down.
  · Step 1 router is three intake-route cards over real radio inputs. The JS contract
    is fixed: data-contact-form, data-role-option, data-role-field and every field
    name are unchanged; contact-form.js reads ?role= and reveals only that group.
  · On a valid submit the form panel is replaced in place by the confirmation state
    (the same trail) — no redirect to a bare thank-you page.

  Kept: front matter, the router JS contract, every field name, the privacy note +
  /privacy-policy/ link, the FAQ. Inputs stay on their solid bg-surface fill
  (THEME.md §5 Contact exception). No map block until the office is confirmed
  visitable (CONTENT.md item 15).
#}

<section class="section-container py-10 sm:py-14">
  {% set crumbs = [{ label: "Home", url: "/" }, { label: "Contact" }] %}
  {% include "partials/breadcrumb.njk" %}

  <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Job seeker or employer — same team</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl font-semibold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
      Contact us.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead-copy mt-5">
      Whether you're looking for a job or looking to hire, we're here to help.
      Fill in the form, or reach us directly — either way the same team picks it up.
    </p>
    {# Presentational only — set by contact-form.js from ?role=, never changes which
       fields are required. #}
    <p class="meta mt-5" data-role-ack hidden></p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start lg:gap-10">

    {# ---- Left — the form ---- #}
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <form data-contact-form novalidate class="glass-panel divide-y divide-ink/10 p-6 sm:p-8">

        {# Step 1 — the router. Three intake routes; each choice swaps in only the
           fields it needs, because every extra field costs submissions. #}
        <fieldset class="pb-7">
          <legend class="meta">Who's asking</legend>
          {% set roles = [
            { value: "job-seeker", label: "Job Seeker", hint: "Resume" },
            { value: "employer", label: "Employer", hint: "Hiring role" },
            { value: "training", label: "Training Applicant", hint: "Choose a track" }
          ] %}
          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-2.5 sm:grid-cols-3">
            {% for role in roles %}
            <label class="block">
              <input type="radio" name="role" value="{{ role.value }}" data-role-option
                     class="peer sr-only" {% if loop.first %}checked{% endif %} required>
              <span class="route-card">
                <span class="route-card-index">
                  0{{ loop.index }}
                  <span class="route-card-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </span>
                <span class="route-card-label">{{ role.label }}</span>
                <span class="route-card-hint">{{ role.hint }}</span>
              </span>
            </label>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        {# Step 2 — your details, plus whatever the chosen role needs alongside them. #}
        <div class="py-7">
          <p class="meta">Your details</p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="name" class="field-label">Full name</label>
              <input type="text" id="name" name="name" class="field" required autocomplete="name">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="email" class="field-label">Email</label>
              <input type="email" id="email" name="email" class="field" required autocomplete="email">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2" data-role-field="employer">
            <div>
              <label for="company" class="field-label">Company name</label>
              <input type="text" id="company" name="company" class="field" autocomplete="organization">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="hiring-for" class="field-label">Role you're hiring for</label>
              <input type="text" id="hiring-for" name="hiring-for" class="field">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-5" data-role-field="job-seeker">
            <label for="resume" class="field-label">Resume upload <span class="normal-case tracking-normal">(PDF or Word)</span></label>
            <input type="file" id="resume" name="resume" accept=".pdf,.doc,.docx"
                   class="field file:mr-4 file:rounded-full file:border-0 file:bg-paper file:px-3 file:py-1.5 file:font-mono file:text-xs file:text-ink">
          </div>

          <div class="mt-5" data-role-field="training">
            <label for="track" class="field-label">Which track interests you?</label>
            <select id="track" name="track" class="field">
              {% for program in programs.list %}
              <option>{{ program.title }}</option>
              {% endfor %}
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>

        {# Step 3 — the message. #}
        <div class="py-7">
          <label for="message" class="meta block">Your message</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="6" class="field mt-4" required
                    placeholder="Describe what you're after — no need to pick a service first, we'll point you to the right one."></textarea>
        </div>

        {# Step 4 — send. #}
        <div class="pt-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
            <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Send Message</button>
            <p class="meta">We reply within one business day.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-5 body-copy text-sm">
            We use your details only to respond to this enquiry. Resumes are shared with
            employers only with your say-so, and we never sell your data. See our
            <a href="{{ '/privacy-policy/' | url }}" class="font-medium text-brand hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </form>

      {# Post-submit confirmation — contact-form.js swaps this in place of the form. #}
      <div data-contact-success hidden class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">Handoff complete</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
          Your enquiry is with the team now.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-6">
          {% set trailNodes = [
            { label: "You sent this", text: "Your enquiry reached the team." },
            { label: "A person has it", text: "Someone reviews it — usually the same day." },
            { label: "We'll reply", text: "You hear from us within one business day." }
          ] %}
          {% include "partials/handoff-trail.njk" %}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 body-copy text-sm">
          If your question is urgent, you can also reach us directly at
          <a href="{{ site.phoneHref }}" class="font-medium text-brand hover:underline">{{ site.phone }}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# ---- Right — the person, kept in view ---- #}
    <div class="lg:col-span-5 lg:sticky lg:top-28">
      <div class="space-y-6">

        <div class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-7">
          <p class="meta">Direct lines</p>
          <dl class="mt-4">
            <div class="fact-row">
              <dt class="meta">Phone</dt>
              <dd><a href="{{ site.phoneHref }}" class="font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:text-brand">{{ site.phone }}</a></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="fact-row">
              <dt class="meta">Email</dt>
              <dd><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:text-brand">{{ site.email }}</a></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="fact-row">
              <dt class="meta">Office</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink/75">{{ site.address.line1 }}, {{ site.address.line2 }}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="fact-row">
              <dt class="meta">Hours</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink/75">{{ site.hours }}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 border-t border-ink/10 pt-4">
            {% for s in site.social %}
            <a href="{{ s.url }}" class="meta transition-colors hover:text-brand">{{ s.label }}</a>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="glass-panel flex gap-4 p-6 sm:p-7">
          <span class="icon-chip icon-chip-accent shrink-0">{{ icon("users", "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
          <div>
            <p class="card-title text-base">A person, not a queue</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5 body-copy text-sm">
              Every enquiry goes straight to the team that handles it — no ticket
              number, no chatbot in between.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-7">
          <p class="meta">What happens next</p>
          <div class="mt-4">
            {% set trailNodes = false %}
            {% include "partials/handoff-trail.njk" %}
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% set faqKey = "contact" %}
{% set faqTitle = "Three quick answers." %}
{% set faqNumbered = true %}
{% include "partials/faq-accordion.njk" %}
